  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared per RBC-RAD-07. Four studies booked (appts 00005, 00003, 00007, 00004); cancelled appts 00006, 00001, 00008 not ordered.\n\n• pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0001): diabetic (diet only); 9/24 creatinine >30 days → pre-scan creatinine ordered (sr-t0005). Late-arriving outside Cr 1.52 (10/22, from 0.94 on 9/24): not AKI by policy definition (28-day interval), eGFR ~64 → no saline; pre-scan creatinine kept; follow-up task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0031). Patient instructed (comm-t0014).\n• pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0002): 2019 day-of radiology report grades iohexol reaction MODERATE (allergy-list \"anaphylaxis, patient report\" does not change grade) → prednisone 50 mg 20:00 Sun/02:00/08:00 Mon (mr-t0007) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 08:00 (mr-t0008); needs driver. Corrected creatinine arrived (10/14 value is 2.8, not 0.98 — specimen mislabel) → eGFR ~24 → added NaCl 0.9% 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0020); corrected bilingual Spanish/English message sent (comm-t0023, original comm-t0013); kidney follow-up task (task-t0026).\n• pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0003): AKI 10/4 ED (Cr 1.24 at discharge, not at baseline, no later Cr) → pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0006), NaCl 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0009), metformin held (mr-00392; last dose Sun evening, off ≥48h after scan, restart only after normal recheck — post-scan creatinine sr-t0011, task-t0012). Late outside report: moderate iopamidol reaction 2022 → prednisone 50 mg 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0021) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 12:00 (mr-t0022), needs driver; updated message (comm-t0024, original comm-t0015). Iopamidol allergy could not be coded from catalog — noted for allergy-list entry.\n• pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00 CT A/P without contrast (sr-t0004): no §1–6 prep; patient told no prep needed (comm-t0016). Late outside report of mild iohexol reaction recorded on allergy list (alg-t0025); no change to plan.\nNotes written for each patient (doc-t0017/18/19/27/28/29/30); the four new inbox items completed. Unrelated pre-existing inbox items left untouched.",
